.TH HMACSHA256TEST 1
.SH NAME
hmacsha256test \- test keyring->hmac_sha256()
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hmacsha256test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Hmacsha256test
checks
.IR keyring (2)'s
.B hmac_sha256()
.RI ( module/keyring.m ,
.IR libinterp/keyring.c ,
.IR libsec/hmac.c )
against four real HMAC-SHA256 test vectors: RFC 4231's own published
test case 1, and three more generated directly from the host's own
.IR openssl (1)
.RB ( "dgst -sha256 -hmac" ),
an independent real implementation, rather than hand-computed or
taken from memory. One vector is the degenerate empty-key/empty-data
case.
.PP
This is the first primitive of the SSL/TLS modernization plan (see
.IR doc/ssl-modernization-plan.md
in the source tree): TLS 1.2's own PRF is HMAC-SHA256 based (RFC 5246
\(sc5), unlike the SSLv3/TLS1.0 PRF
.IR module/ssl3.m
already implements, which mixes MD5 and SHA1 directly rather than
using HMAC at all.
.PP
Exits with
.B PASS
if every vector matched, or
.B FAIL
naming which case, the expected digest, and the digest actually
computed.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/hmacsha256test.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR keyring (2)
.SH BUGS
Four vectors, not an exhaustive test suite; RFC 4231's remaining test
cases (including the ones exercising key lengths past the HMAC block
size) are not included.
